WEBVTT

1
0:00:05.132 --> 0:00:10.509
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> We all know that too much sugar and salt isn’t good for us.

2
0:00:10.708 --> 0:00:18.858
But do we really know how much sugar and salt are in some of the things we eat and drink every day?

3
0:00:19.639 --> 0:00:22.013
Let’s start with sugar.

4
0:00:22.887 --> 0:00:33.058
According to the American Heart Association, the maximum healthy limit for a woman is twenty-four grams of sugar a day.

5
0:00:33.273 --> 0:00:36.383
That’s just six teaspoons.

6
0:00:37.057 --> 0:00:44.103
For a man it is no more than thirty-six grams, which is nine teaspoons.

7
0:00:45.237 --> 0:00:55.332
Here we have an egg, a can of coke, a small bar of dark chocolate, and an apple.

8
0:00:56.282 --> 0:01:00.311
How much sugar do you think they contain?

9
0:01:01.276 --> 0:01:05.535
One of them has thirty-five grams of sugar.

10
0:01:06.025 --> 0:01:12.045
That’s eleven grams more than the healthy limit for a woman in a day.

11
0:01:12.888 --> 0:01:15.890
Which one do you think it is?

12
0:01:16.825 --> 0:01:28.559
Yes, it’s the can of coke. A can of Coke has approximately thirty-five grams of sugar. That is a lot.

13
0:01:30.244 --> 0:01:33.308
And which has no sugar at all?

14
0:01:34.840 --> 0:01:37.643
Of course, it’s the egg.

15
0:01:38.333 --> 0:01:41.151
So what about the other two?

16
0:01:41.672 --> 0:01:48.872
Which do you think has more sugar, the chocolate or the apple?

17
0:01:49.500 --> 0:01:52.733
Surprisingly, it’s the apple.

18
0:01:53.192 --> 0:02:00.790
The apple has approximately twenty-three grams of sugar. That’s quite a lot.

19
0:02:01.112 --> 0:02:12.801
But it’s fructose, a natural sugar. And remember that fruit is also good for you, as it contains vitamin C.

20
0:02:13.766 --> 0:02:20.261
The chocolate bar only has a little sugar, just ten grams.

21
0:02:20.613 --> 0:02:27.783
But remember, it’s dark chocolate, and it’s only a small bar.

22
0:02:29.268 --> 0:02:35.197
What about salt? How much salt can we eat in a day?

23
0:02:36.009 --> 0:02:40.405
This time it’s the same for men and women.

24
0:02:40.896 --> 0:02:45.231
The answer is no more than six grams.

25
0:02:46.395 --> 0:02:58.512
Here we have a small packet of crisps, a bottle of olive oil, a bottle of mineral water and a piece of bread.

26
0:02:59.753 --> 0:03:09.634
So how much salt do they contain? Which one has a lot of salt, and which one has none?

27
0:03:10.323 --> 0:03:18.458
You may be surprised to hear that the one with a lot of salt is the piece of white bread.

28
0:03:18.994 --> 0:03:23.498
It has approximately nought point five grams.

29
0:03:24.371 --> 0:03:28.231
And which one has no salt at all?

30
0:03:28.492 --> 0:03:34.972
No, it’s not the mineral water, it’s the olive oil.

31
0:03:35.554 --> 0:03:43.964
It contains no salt at all, and as part of a Mediterranean diet, it’s very healthy.

32
0:03:44.807 --> 0:03:47.242
So what about the other two.

33
0:03:47.978 --> 0:03:55.132
Well, a small packet of crisps has approximately nought point three four grams of salt.

34
0:03:55.729 --> 0:04:06.085
And lastly, there is a little salt in the mineral water. Just nought point nought nought two three grams.

35
0:04:06.820 --> 0:04:15.659
So when you’re shopping, how do you know what to buy to make sure it doesn’t have too much sugar or salt?

36
0:04:16.195 --> 0:04:24.621
The answer is, always check the list of ingredients, and remember what your daily limit is.